A copy, or a delete's children, put after a slot
without the successor's predecessor moving to the last of them
leaves that link on a node whose next is no longer the successor.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: predecessor's next is not the slot
Witness: fuzz actor-handoff

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -100,7 +100,6 @@ void cap_attach(struct cap *parent, struct cap *n)
 /* Put the siblings first to last right after beside, which has a parent, in its ring. */
 static void splice_after(struct cap *beside, struct cap *first, struct cap *last)
 {
-    cap_set_prev(ring_next(beside), v2p(last));
     cap_set_next(last, cap_next(beside));
     cap_set_prev(first, v2p(beside));
     cap_set_next(beside, v2p(first));
